<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria Montessori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a>–<a href="/years/1952">1952</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria Montessori was an Italian physician and educator who developed the Montessori method of teaching. She opened her first Casa dei Bambini (Children's House) in a working-class district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1907, basing it on children's self-directed activity with specially designed materials. Her method spread worldwide; she left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a> in the 1930s and spent her later years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-montessori.jpg" alt="Maria Montessori" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maria_Montessori_(portrait).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
